    "Restrict the compact critical-hexagon parameter family to positive orientation. Shared first midpoints have the same six midpoint coordinates. The first-midpoint projection is a compact quotient map, so the next-midpoint map is continuous on the actual critical midpoint locus. Rotating the labels proves that its second successor is next(p)-p, its third is -p, and its sixth is p. Thus successor is a homeomorphism, all six midpoint coordinates vary continuously, and det(p,next(p))=sqrt(3)/2. No full-boundary coverage or cyclic monotonicity is assumed.",
