    "A normalized support form for any boundary point also supports a critical midpoint in its face. Uniqueness at that midpoint identifies the form with the side normal of a critical hexagon. Thus every boundary point lies on an edge of a critical hexagon: criticalContactSet equals the entire frontier. This does not yet assert that every boundary point is a side midpoint.",
